MODULE 03 — MODES: DARK MODE & COLOR INVERSION

Create a new primary navigation section named:

Modes

This section will contain two independent controls:

1. Dark Mode
2. Color Inversion

The two systems must remain completely separate in terms of UI, state management, preferences, and actual functionality.

1. Dark Mode

Create a dedicated Dark Mode section.

The intention is to manage dark appearance independently wherever the Android platform and individual applications genuinely support it.

Requirements:

- Identify applications for which a genuine supported per-app Dark Mode mechanism exists.
- Display only applications for which RESOLVE can actually perform the requested operation.
- Show the application's icon and name.
- Provide an independent Dark Mode control for each supported application.
- Save each application's preference independently.
- Restore the saved preference when RESOLVE is reopened.
- Verify that the requested change was actually applied.

Do not assume that all Android applications support external Dark Mode control.

Do not implement a fake Dark Mode switch.

Do not use an unsupported hidden API or pretend that changing RESOLVE's own theme changes the theme of other applications.

IMPORTANT TECHNICAL CONSTRAINT:

Android's public "UiModeManager.setApplicationNightMode()" controls the application that calls it. It does not provide a general API for an ordinary third-party application to change the Night Mode of arbitrary installed applications.

Therefore:

- Inspect the existing implementation.
- Identify any legitimate device-specific or officially supported per-app control mechanism.
- Use only mechanisms that are genuinely supported and authorized.
- Do not misrepresent system-wide Dark Mode as per-app Dark Mode.

If an application cannot be controlled independently, do not include it in the supported selectable list.

If an unavailable or previously supported item is selected and its operation fails, display a brief, clear message:

"Dark Mode is not supported for this app on this device."

The application must never report success unless the state was actually changed and verified.

2. Color Inversion

Create an entirely separate Color Inversion section inside Modes.

This must not share its state with Dark Mode.

Requirements:

- Analyze whether genuine per-app Color Inversion is supported.
- Display only applications for which a legitimate per-app implementation is available.
- Maintain independent preferences for each supported application.
- Verify whether the selected change actually takes effect.
- Handle unsupported operations without pretending success.

IMPORTANT:

Android's standard Accessibility Color Inversion setting is a device-wide display setting, not a general per-app inversion API.

Do not silently change the entire device's display colors while presenting the action as an individual application's Color Inversion.

Do not modify secure system settings through unauthorized methods.

If per-app inversion is unavailable on the current device:

- Do not create fake per-app switches.
- Do not list unsupported applications as controllable.
- Display a concise explanation that per-app inversion is unavailable.
- If an attempted operation fails, show:

"Color Inversion is not supported for this app on this device."

If a manufacturer provides a legitimate, supported per-app display-control capability, inspect and use it only when its operation can be verified.

3. Independent State Management

This requirement is particularly important.

Dark Mode and Color Inversion must have separate state and preference storage.

Conceptually maintain separate mappings:

- "darkModePreferences[packageName]"
- "colorInversionPreferences[packageName]"

Do not connect one preference to the other.

Examples:

- Enabling Dark Mode must NOT automatically enable Color Inversion.
- Disabling Dark Mode must NOT disable Color Inversion.
- Enabling Color Inversion must NOT automatically change Dark Mode.
- Changing one application must NOT change the preferences of another application.

A selected Dark Mode preference must not trigger any inversion operation.

A selected Color Inversion preference must not trigger any Dark Mode operation.

